==English==
===Etymology===
Late {{inh|en|enm|-}}, from {{der|en|LL.|sciatica}}, feminine of {{m|la|sciaticus}}, from {{der|en|grc|ἰσχιαδικός}}, the adjective of {{m|grc|ἰσχίον||hip}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/saɪˈætɪkə/}}
* {{hyphenation|en|sci|at|i|ca}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|pathology|neurology}} [[neuralgia|Neuralgia]] of the [[sciatic nerve]], characterised by pain radiating down through the buttocks and the back of the thigh.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|sciatic}}

